Falsifies `system_tests::user::raw_mode_tests::a_badged_copy_of_the_terminal_reads_keystrokes_and_cannot_type_them`.

Architecture: all three (the change is in a userspace component, `components/src/line_editor.rs`,
built for every ISA from one source).

The defect this restores is the one milestone 709 closes: the boot line discipline served every
request the same whatever the badge on the capability that sent it, so a `graphical_terminal`
session holding a copy of its endpoint could `OP_BYTES` a command line into the queue the boot shell
reads with `OP_READLINE`. The patch removes the badge guard ahead of `match proto::op(w0)` and the
`badge` binding it reads (so the build stays warning-free).

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!(r[0], BAD_REQUEST, "a badged holder's OP_BYTES was served (r0 = 0):
it can type a line the boot shell reads")`, the first assertion in the test. Under the patch the
discipline answers `0` and queues `ls`.

Replayed on 2026-10-03 (UTC) by the lane for milestone 709 (a graphical terminal session on the
no-keyboard arm holds only the raw half of the boot discipline); see the roadmap block for the exit
code and the assertion line. The first red was taken before the fix existed, which is the same
tree as this patch applied.

